.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Unit tests for the 42sh lexer module\&. 

Covers lexer_tokenize(), is_operator(), is_operator_start(), read_word(), read_operator(), token_new(), and lexer_free_tokens()\&.
.SS "How to enable"
Add \fR-DTEST_LEXER_ENABLED\fP to \fRTEST_FLAGS\fP in the root Makefile and declare \fR\fBtest_lexer_suite\fP\fP in \fBtest_runner\&.c\fP\&. Once all assertions are permanently green, remove the \fR#ifdef\fP guards and the \fR-D\fP flag per the workflow described in \fBtest_runner\&.c\fP\&.
.SS "Sections"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBtoken_new\fP — allocation and field initialisation
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBis_operator / is_operator_start\fP — character classification
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBread_word\fP — word boundary detection, quote handling, backslash escapes
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBread_operator\fP — every operator token type
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBlexer_tokenize\fP — end-to-end tokenisation of realistic shell inputs 
.PP

.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "t_token * nth_token (t_list * head, int n)\fR [static]\fP"

.PP
Return the nth token (0-based) from a token list\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIhead\fP Head of the list returned by lexer_tokenize()\&. 
.br
\fIn\fP Zero-based index of the desired node\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
Pointer to the t_token, or NULL if the list is shorter than n\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void test_lexer_suite (void )"

.PP
Run all lexer unit tests\&. Called by \fBtest_runner\&.c\fP via MU_RUN(test_lexer_suite)\&. 
.SS "void test_read_operator_io_number (void )\fR [static]\fP"

.PP
read_operator extracts an io_number from a digit-prefixed redirect\&. "2>" must produce TOK_REDIR_OUT with io_number == 2\&. 
.SS "void test_read_word_backslash_escape (void )\fR [static]\fP"

.PP
read_word respects a backslash-escaped space outside quotes\&. "hello\\ world" should be consumed as a single token\&. 
.SS "void test_read_word_single_quote (void )\fR [static]\fP"

.PP
read_word includes the entire single-quoted span as one token\&. Spaces inside single quotes must not terminate the word\&. 
.SS "void test_token_new_basic (void )\fR [static]\fP"

.PP
token_new allocates a node and sets all three fields correctly\&. Verifies that the returned list node is non-NULL, that its content pointer is non-NULL, and that type, value, and io_number match the arguments\&. 
.SS "void test_tokenize_io_number (void )\fR [static]\fP"

.PP
A digit-prefixed redirect stores the correct io_number on the token\&. "cmd 2>>err" must produce io_number == 2 on the TOK_REDIR_APPEND token\&. 
.SS "void test_tokenize_quoted_operators (void )\fR [static]\fP"

.PP
Quoted strings containing operators are treated as a single WORD\&. "echo '|; <>'" must not produce any operator tokens\&. 
.SS "void test_tokenize_whitespace_trimmed (void )\fR [static]\fP"

.PP
Leading and trailing spaces are ignored\&. "  echo  " should yield the same token stream as "echo"\&. 
